        "original_id": "785ba469-7409-5a54-9cc1-59bd1a1f4cdc",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Max Hoffmann, Paul von Hindenburg, Erich Ludendorff\n- Events: Battle of Tannenberg, First Battle of the Masurian Lakes, Battle of Liège, Treaty of Brest-Litovsk\n- Roles: German general, commander of German forces in the east, chief negotiator\n\nFacts:\n- Erich Ludendorff was a German general who lived from 9 April 1865 to 20 December 1937.\n- Erich Ludendorff was regarded as the victor of the Battle of Liège and the Battle of Tannenberg.\n- Max Hoffmann, together with Paul von Hindenburg and Erich Ludendorff, masterminded the devastating defeat of the Russian armies at Tannenberg and the Masurian Lakes.\n- Max Hoffmann served as a chief negotiator in the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk.\n- During the period described in relation to the Polish–Soviet War in 1919, Max Hoffmann was the commander of the German forces in the east and was facing increasing difficulties.",
